{
  "title": "Namaz of Imam al-Hadi (a.s.)",
  "data": "Upon concluding the prayer, say the following supplication:\nيَا بَارُّ يَا وَصُولُ\nYAA BAARRU YAA WASOOL\nO Foremost Beneficent! O Object of Love!\nيَا شَاهِدَ كُلِّ غَائِبٍ\nYAA SHAAHIDA KULLI GHAA'IB\nO He Who is the Witness of all unseen things!\nوَيَا قَريبُ غَيْرُ بَعِيدٍ\nWA YAA QAREEBU GHAYRU BA'EED\nO He Who is Nigh without being away (from any other thing)!\nوَيَا غَالِبُ غَيْرُ مَغْلُوبٍ\nWA YAA GHAALIBU GHAYRU MAGHLOOB\nO He Who (always) prevails (but) is never overpowered!\nوَيَا مَنْ لَا يَعْلَمُ كَيْفَ هُوَ اِلَّا هُوَ\nWA YAA MAN LAA YA'LAMU KAYFA HUWA ILLAA HUW\nO He Whom no one knows how He is except He!\nيَا مَنْ لَا تُبْلَغُ قُدْرَتُهٗ\nYAA MAN LAA TUBLAGHU QUDRATUH\nO He Whose authority no one can challenge!\nاَسْاَلُكَ اللَّهُمَّ بِاسْمِكَ الْمَكْنُونِ الْمَخْزُونِ\nAS'ALUKAL LAAHUMMA BISMIKAL MAKNOONIL MAKHZOON\nI beseech You, O Allah, in Your name: the Well-Guarded, the Treasured,\nالْمَكْتُومِ عَمَّنْ شِئْتَ\nAL-MAKTOOMI A'MMAN SHI'T\nthe Concealed from whom You will,\nالطَّاهِرِ الْمُطَهَّرِ الْمُقَدَّسِ\nAT-TAAHIRIL MUTAHHARIL MUQADDAS\nthe Pure, the Purified, the Holy,\nالنُّورِ التَّامِّ\nAN-NOORIT TAAMM\nthe utter Light,\nالْحَيِّ الْقَيُّومِ الْعَظِيمِ\nAL-HAYYIL QAYYOOMIL A'ZEEM\nthe Ever-living, the Everlasting, the Greatest,\nنُورِ السَّمَاوَاتِ وَنُورِ الْاَرَضِينَ\nNOORIS SAMAAWAATI WA NOORIL ARADEEN\nthe Light of the heavens and the Light of the [layers of the] earth,\nعَالِمِ الْغَيْبِ وَالشَّهَادَةِ\nA'ALIMIL GHAYBI WASH SHAHAADAH\nthe Knower of the unseen and the seen\nالْكَبِيرِ الْمُتَعَالِ الْعَظِيمِ\nAL-KABEERIL MUTA'AALIL A'ZEEM\nthe Highest, the Sublime, the Glorious!\nصَلِّ عَلَىٰ مُحَمَّدٍ وَآلِ مُحَمَّدٍ\nSALLI A'LAA MUHAMMADIN WA AALI MUHAMMAD\nSend blessings upon Muhammad and the Household of Muhammad.",
  "merits": "In his book of Jamal al-Usbu', Sayyid Ibn Tawus has recorded a special prayer and supplication for each of the Holy Imams (a.s.), to be offered on Fridays.\nImam al-Hadi (a.s.)'s prayer consists of two units. In the first unit, recite [Surah al-Fatihah](A5) and [Surah Ya-Sin](A40); in the second, [Surah al-Fatihah](A5) and [Surah al-Rahman](A59)."
}
